## Decision required — read this before starting

The design's primary CTA is **"Style an outfit with this"** (`:654`). That conflicts with Decision 5
(CLAUDE.md): looks are a daily drop, generated once per local day, and tapping an occasion reads stored
rows without calling the model. Styling around a chosen item is inherently on demand.

**This plan assumes the cheap reading**, and Task 5 is written against it:

> Tapping filters **today's already-stored looks** to those containing this item and opens the first
> match. If none contain it, the button offers *"Build a look around this"*, which runs a real
> generation and **consumes the regenerate quota** (`lib/outfits/quota.ts`).

That keeps the free tier free, honours Decision 5, and gives the quota seam its first real consumer.
The alternative — an AI call on every tap — would make this button the largest per-user cost in the
product. **If you want that instead, change Task 5 before implementing it, not after.**

Second assumption: **prices are GBP**, formatted with `Intl.NumberFormat("en-GB")`, because the design
prices Pro at `£5/mo` and shows `£3.28` cost-per-wear. A currency setting belongs to the Settings plan;
until it exists, one hard-coded currency beats a fake one.

