The design's four toggles (`docs/prototype-review.md` §12): **Daily fit reminder · Rain guard · Auto-log
worn looks · Metric units & °C**.

## Scope decisions

| Toggle | Decision |
|---|---|
| **Rain guard** ("never suede in rain") | **Ship it.** `weatherRules` already excludes suede and canvas when it rains — this switch turns that off, which is a two-line change and the only toggle whose behaviour already exists. |
| **Auto-log worn looks** | **Ship it.** Read by the daily-drop path: when on, opening a look after 18:00 local logs it. Needs the wear-logging plan. |
| **Daily fit reminder** | **Do not ship.** It needs web-push, which CLAUDE.md defers to Phase 2. Rendering a switch that schedules nothing is the lie this plan is trying to avoid. |
| **Metric units & °C** | **Do not ship as a toggle.** Open-Meteo is requested in °C and every surface assumes it. Show the current unit as a read-only row until an imperial path exists. |
| **Language EN · DE** | **Render, disabled.** next-intl is deferred; the control shows EN selected with DE marked "Soon". |

That leaves **two live toggles**. Fewer switches that work beats four that mostly do not.

